{#
  Filename kept in French, as it was first written -- the same precedent
  `docs/handbook/governance/traitement-donnees.md` already set, registered in
  `app/src/content/registry.ts` under the English key
  `governance/data-protection-record`, whose own comment says the same
  thing: every other file in that directory is named in English. This
  page's own address follows the site's own English convention the same
  way that registry key does: /data/, not /donnees/.

  This page cites the data-protection record rather than restating
  it -- in particular, it never repeats the retention figure that record
  gives, on purpose: two documents stating the same number independently
  will disagree the day one of them is updated and the other is not.
  `tools/tests/repository/test_site.py`'s archive section pins the link below against
  the same two constants that decide where the record actually lands
  (`app/src/content/registry.ts`'s own file path, `app/vite.config.ts`'s
  own published base), rather than against a literal URL nothing would
  catch drifting.
#}
<section class="hero">
  {% if motif.pieces %}{{ heroPieces(motif) }}{% endif %}
  <div class="container hero__inner">
    <p class="hero__eyebrow">Data &amp; privacy</p>
    <h1 class="hero__title">What we hold, <em>and for how long.</em></h1>
    <p class="hero__lede">
      Registering for a seminar and receiving a certificate involve a
      small amount of personal data. You can read exactly what we hold,
      and ask us to change or delete it.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section container">
  {% if motif.pieces %}{{ piece(motif, "below-band") }}{% endif %}
